gnmic-rs is an independent Rust re-implementation of the gNMI dial-out
collector of gnmic. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by or supported by
Nokia, Google or the OpenConfig project. "gnmic" is used only to describe
compatibility.

This product includes or is derived from the following Apache-2.0 licensed
works:

* gnmic - https://github.com/openconfig/gnmic
  Copyright Nokia and the gNMIc contributors.
  Portions of the configuration handling, xpath <-> gNMI path conversion,
  subscription request building, event model and output formatting were
  translated from Go to Rust and modified (src/config.rs, src/path.rs,
  src/subscribe.rs, src/event.rs, src/format.rs). Configuration key names and
  the json/event output formats follow gnmic's.

* gNMI protocol definitions - https://github.com/openconfig/gnmi
  Copyright 2016-2018 Google Inc.
  proto/gnmi.proto (modified: import path of gnmi_ext.proto) and
  proto/gnmi_ext.proto (unmodified).

* grpctunnel protocol definition - https://github.com/openconfig/grpctunnel
  Copyright 2019 Google Inc.
  proto/tunnel.proto (unmodified). src/tunnel.rs implements this protocol.
